# ChatGPT / Claude web — Channel Creator MCP (remote)

Remote hosts use Streamable HTTP on **:8411** (`oauth` / `dual` / `bearer`).
**Never** tunnel StreamTV **:8410**.

## Start on the Mac

```bash
export STREAMTV_MCP_AUTH=dual
export STREAMTV_MCP_TOKEN="$(openssl rand -hex 32)"
export STREAMTV_MCP_ACCESS_TEAM=myteam
export STREAMTV_MCP_ACCESS_AUDIENCE="<AUD tag>"

__PYTHON__ -m mcp_streamtv.main \
  --transport http --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8411 \
  --auth dual --profile guided
```

## Tunnel checklist

```bash
zsh scripts/channel_creator_mcp_remote.zsh
# optional: --public-url https://YOUR_HOST/mcp
```

## Values to type in ChatGPT / Claude web

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| MCP URL | `https://YOUR_HOST/mcp` |
| Auth (oauth) | Sign in with Auth0 / Cloudflare Access |
| Auth (dual Lock 1) | Cloudflare Access on the hostname |
| Auth (dual Lock 2) | Bearer token = `STREAMTV_MCP_TOKEN` |

Repo: `__REPO_ROOT__`  
Local API (not tunneled): `__BASE_URL__`

